{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>for it is double the wages of a hired worker.</b> (A hired worker's wage is) three years — as in 'the years of a hired worker' and 'the slighting of the pride of Moab.' If so, this one who serves six years constitutes double that of a hired worker. Therefore they adopted the practice for a hired worker of three years: for were they to hire for one year or two, sometimes there is a revai-year and sometimes there is not, and one party would end up losing. But with three years, it cannot be without a revai-year, and neither this one nor that one loses."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The phrase in parentheses, שכיר שכר הוא, appears parenthetical and possibly gloss-like; its meaning is uncertain. The reference is to Isaiah 16:14 and 21:16, where 'the years of a hired worker' is three years. עבור likely refers to a year of agricultural activity (plowing/sowing), here linked to the revai cycle of shemittah."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:03.379305683Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}